[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 3. **Perturb(D) -> A:1 B:0 C:1 D:0**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m We must check whether these observations are consistent with the candidate graph.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m **Step 1: Understand the semantics**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - A node is **0** if it is not a downstream descendant of the perturbed node.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - A node is **1** if it is a downstream descendant of the perturbed node.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - A node is **0** otherwise.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m **Step 2: Analyze each perturbation**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
