[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m **1. Perturb(A):**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - A is the perturbed node, so A:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - The graph does not have any edges pointing to A, so no other node can influence A.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - The graph has no edges from A to any other node, so none of B, C, or D can influence A.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - Therefore, B:0, C:0, D:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - This matches the observed result: A:0, B:0, C:1, D:0 → **Contradiction**.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - **This is inconsistent.**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m **2. Perturb(B):**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - B is the perturbed node, so B:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - From the graph, B -> A, B -> C, B -> D.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - So, A, C, D are descendants of B.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - Therefore, A:1, C:1, D:1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - The observed result is: A:1, B:0, C:1, D:1 → **This matches.**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
