[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - D is the perturbed node, so D:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - From the graph, D -> A, D -> C.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - So, A and C are descendants of D.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - Therefore, A:1, C:1, D:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - The observed result is: A:1, B:0, C:1, D:0 → **This matches.**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m ### Conclusion:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=682122)[0m - The perturbation of A leads to an inconsistency, as C is observed to be 1, but in the graph, C is not a descendant of A.
